  "intro": "Essential information The coca leaf is much more than a plant in Peru: it is a cultural symbol, medicine […]",
  "content_html": "\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"informaci-on-esencial\"> Essential information</h2>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://old.culturademontania.org.ar/Arqueologia/hojacoca1.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://old.culturademontania.org.ar/Arqueologia/hojacoca1.jpg\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/976/cpsprodpb/C6D6/production/_83920905_04658d29-81c4-42ce-8e38-3709df6a473d.jpg\" class=\"wp-image-838\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"549\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/83920905_04658d29-81c4-42ce-8e38-3709df6a473d-9a34d6e1e4.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/83920905_04658d29-81c4-42ce-8e38-3709df6a473d-9a34d6e1e4-640.webp 640w, images/blog/content/83920905_04658d29-81c4-42ce-8e38-3709df6a473d-9a34d6e1e4.webp 976w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"976\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://ayahuasca-wachuma.com/assets/images/ceremonies/coca-leaf-oracle-ceremony-cusco.webp\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://ayahuasca-wachuma.com/assets/images/ceremonies/coca-leaf-oracle-ceremony-cusco.webp\"/></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong>coca leaf</strong> It is much more than a plant in Peru: it is <strong>cultural symbol, ancestral medicine and living tradition</strong> dating back thousands of years. Used since the time of the Inca Empire, coca has accompanied Andean communities in their daily, spiritual and social lives.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, it remains a fundamental part of Peruvian identity, especially in regions such as Cusco, Puno and the Amazon.<br/><br/><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/reel/2153478802129489\">Watch Video</a></p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"datos-clave\"> Key data</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> <strong>Scientific name:</strong> <em>Erythroxylum coca</em><br/> <strong>Origin:</strong> Amazonian Andes<br/> <strong>Traditional use:</strong> chewed (acullico), infusions (coca mate)<br/> <strong>Status:</strong> legal in its traditional form in Peru<br/> <strong>Altitude:</strong> 500 – 2000 m.a.s.l.<br/> <strong>Properties:</strong> natural energizer, helps against altitude sickness</p>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"una-historia-que-empieza-en-las-monta-nas\"> A story that begins in the mountains</h2>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://larepublica.cronosmedia.glr.pe/original/2024/11/08/672e33d5e2dcb85f6f162a18.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://larepublica.cronosmedia.glr.pe/original/2024/11/08/672e33d5e2dcb85f6f162a18.jpg\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://cdn.biodiversidadla.org/var/biodiversidadla_org/storage/images/documentos/la-hoja-de-coca-en-las-comunidades-andinas/1328627-1-esl-ES/La-hoja-de-coca-en-las-comunidades-andinas_full.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://cdn.biodiversidadla.org/var/biodiversidadla_org/storage/images/documentos/la-hoja-de-coca-en-las-comunidades-andinas/1328627-1-esl-ES/La-hoja-de-coca-en-las-comunidades-andinas_full.jpg\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://www.peru.travel/Contenido/General/Imagen/es/1406/1.1/turistas-en-zona-arqueologica-moray-cusco-desktop.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.peru.travel/Contenido/General/Imagen/es/1406/1.1/turistas-en-zona-arqueologica-moray-cusco-desktop.jpg\"/></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Imagine this: you are high in the Andes, the air is cold, the silence is deep... and someone next to you takes out some small green leaves.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It's not coffee.<br/>It is not an energy drink.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is <strong>coca leaf</strong> </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The same one that accompanied the wise men of the Inca Empire, the same one that is still alive today in communities in Cusco and beyond.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But here comes the interesting thing:<br/> What the world thinks it knows about coca... is incomplete.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"no-es-lo-que-piensas-y-eso-lo-cambia-todo\"> It's not what you think (and that changes everything)</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For decades, the coca leaf has been misunderstood.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many automatically associate it with something negative.<br/>But in its natural state, it is quite the opposite:</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> It's medicine<br/> It's tradition<br/> It's identity</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The difference is in something key:<br/> <strong>The natural leaf is NOT the same as its processed derivatives</strong></p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And understanding that completely changes the story.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"el-ritual-silencioso-que-te-conecta-con-la-tierra\"> The silent ritual that connects you to the earth</h2>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://tn.com.ar/resizer/v2/ritual-del-pago-a-la-tierra-en-la-isla-taquile-en-el-lago-titicaca-foto-promperu- MNUWOJONVJCBVBIINW5H7EZNPE.jpeg?auth=e0982f2a788785fada737e6618164ff76bdba2e7df9a1180a8937d4d4f13dec8&amp;width=767\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://tn.com.ar/resizer/v2/ritual-del-pago-a-la-tierra-en-la-isla-taquile-en-el-lago-titicaca-foto-promperu-MNUWOJONVJCBVBIINW5H7EZNPE.jpeg?auth=e0982f2a788785fada737e6618164ff76bdba2e7df9a1180a8937d4d4f13dec8&amp;width=767\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://www.huillcaexpedition.com/images/blog/md/el-ritual-ancestral-del-pago-a-la-tierra-1686012609.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.huillcaexpedition.com/images/blog/md/el-ritual-ancestral-del-pago-a-la-tierra-1686012609.jpg\"/></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In the Andes, coca is not consumed… <strong>is respected</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before chewing it, many pause.<br/>They select the best leaves.<br/>They offer them first to Pachamama </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This small gesture says it all:<br/> There is no rush here, there is connection.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The coca leaf is part of ceremonies, important decisions and moments of introspection.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is literally a conversation with nature.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"para-qu-e-se-usa-la-hoja-de-coca\"> What is the coca leaf used for?</h2>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"consumo-tradicional-acullico-y-mate\"> Traditional consumption (acullico and mate)</h3>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Mate_de_coca_boliviano.jpg\" class=\"wp-image-842\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1707\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/mate_de_coca_boliviano-scaled-4c2bab71c8.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/mate_de_coca_boliviano-scaled-4c2bab71c8-640.webp 640w, images/blog/content/mate_de_coca_boliviano-scaled-4c2bab71c8-1024.webp 1024w, images/blog/content/mate_de_coca_boliviano-scaled-4c2bab71c8.webp 1400w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"2560\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://http2.mlstatic.com/D_NQ_NP_621326-MPE86626415307_062025-O.webp\" class=\"wp-image-839\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"490\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/d_nq_np_621326-mpe86626415307_062025-o-fbe86a4097.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/d_nq_np_621326-mpe86626415307_062025-o-fbe86a4097.webp 500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"500\"/></figure>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Ancestral chew (acullico) for energy </li>\n<li>Hot infusion (coca mate) </li>\n<li>Reduces fatigue and hunger</li>\n<li>Helps combat <strong>soroche (altitude sickness)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> It is common for tourists in Cusco to consume it upon arrival.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"uso-espiritual-y-ceremonial\"> Spiritual and ceremonial use</h3>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://ayahuasca-wachuma.com/assets/images/ceremonies/coca-leaf-reading-in-cusco-shaman.webp\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://ayahuasca-wachuma.com/assets/images/ceremonies/coca-leaf-reading-in-cusco-shaman.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://old.culturademontania.org.ar/Arqueologia/ofrenda_pachamama_hoja_coca_1.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://old.culturademontania.org.ar/Arqueologia/ofrenda_pachamama_hoja_coca_1.jpg\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Curandero_andino_Asencio_Noa_leyendo_la_hoja_de_coca.jpg/250px-Curandero_andino_Asencio_Noa_leyendo_la_hoja_de_coca.jpg\" class=\"wp-image-837\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"375\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/250px-curandero_andino_asencio_noa_leyendo_la_hoja_de_coca-2f9fbf9d3a.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/250px-curandero_andino_asencio_noa_leyendo_la_hoja_de_coca-2f9fbf9d3a.webp 250w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"250\"/></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Offerings to Pachamama </li>\n<li>Leaf reading (spiritual interpretation)</li>\n<li>Ritual of gratitude and connection</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Coca is considered <strong>sacred plant</strong> in the Andean worldview.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"uso-medicinal-natural\"> Natural medicinal use</h3>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://tikafarma.com/cdn/shop/products/hoja-coca-amazon-andes-1.jpg?v=1656620850&amp;width=1200\" class=\"wp-image-840\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1200\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/hoja-coca-amazon-andes-1-65ee42651b.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/hoja-coca-amazon-andes-1-65ee42651b-640.webp 640w, images/blog/content/hoja-coca-amazon-andes-1-65ee42651b-1024.webp 1024w, images/blog/content/hoja-coca-amazon-andes-1-65ee42651b.webp 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"1200\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://acdn-us.mitiendanube.com/stores/001/054/513/products/coca-propiedades1-b9ecb1c9c8693ed82f15780222205778-1024-1024.webp\" class=\"wp-image-836\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"images/blog/content/coca-propiedades1-b9ecb1c9c8693ed82f15780222205778-1024-1024-a5df4ce97a.webp\" srcset=\"images/blog/content/coca-propiedades1-b9ecb1c9c8693ed82f15780222205778-1024-1024-a5df4ce97a-640.webp 640w, images/blog/content/coca-propiedades1-b9ecb1c9c8693ed82f15780222205778-1024-1024-a5df4ce97a.webp 958w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 900px\" width=\"958\"/></figure>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Improves digestion</li>\n<li>Relieves minor pain</li>\n<li>Increases physical resistance</li>\n<li>Reduces effects of cold and altitude</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Used for generations without processed chemicals.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"es-legal-la-hoja-de-coca\"> Is the coca leaf legal?</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, <strong>In its natural form it is legal in Peru</strong> </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Allowed for traditional consumption<br/> Sale in local markets<br/> Protected cultural use</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> What is illegal is your <strong>drug processing</strong></p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> It is important to differentiate the natural plant from its processed derivatives.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"d-onde-se-cultiva-en-per-u\"> Where is it grown in Peru?</h2>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://content-historia.nationalgeographic.com.es/medio/2022/09/15/pisaq_6fbede48_1200x630.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://content-historia.nationalgeographic.com.es/medio/2022/09/15/pisaq_6fbede48_1200x630.jpeg\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://imagenes.elpais.com/resizer/v2/RVI6ZMRQ2M7HENUXTH2JSDBZKQ.jpg?auth=a4f7ea5597903df5467955e94b89208cede93d6a2ab4a4a82bf36723059e50f0&amp;width=1200\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://imagenes.elpais.com/resizer/v2/RVI6ZMRQ2M7HENUXTH2JSDBZKQ.jpg?auth=a4f7ea5597903df5467955e94b89208cede93d6a2ab4a4a82bf36723059e50f0&amp;width=1200\"/></figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img alt=\"https://previews.123rf.com/images/mrpeak/mrpeak1705/mrpeak170500004/78284211-dried-coca-leaves-as-background-in-peru-coca-leaves-are-drunk-as-tea-or-traditionally-chewed-in-the.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://previews.123rf.com/images/mrpeak/mrpeak1705/mrpeak170500004/78284211-dried-coca-leaves-as-background-in-peru-coca-leaves-are-drunk-as-tea-or-traditionally-chewed-in-the.jpg\"/></figure>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The main growing areas include:</p>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li> Valley of the Apurímac, Ene and Mantaro rivers (VRAEM)</li>\n<li> Andean and Amazonian regions</li>\n<li> Peruvian high jungle</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Many communities depend on this crop in a traditional way.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"cu-ando-consumirla\"> When to consume it?</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> When reaching high altitude areas<br/> During walks or trekking <br/> In cold climates <br/> After heavy meals</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> Ideal for travelers on routes such as Machu Picchu or trekking in the Andes.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recomendaciones-importantes\"> Important recommendations</h2>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li> Consume in moderation</li>\n<li> Do not take it outside the country (it may be illegal)</li>\n<li> Avoid in young children</li>\n<li> Check if you are pregnant</li>\n<li> Get informed before traveling</li>\n</ul>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"cultura-viva-del-per-u\"> Living culture of Peru</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The coca leaf is not just a plant: it is <strong>history, identity and cultural resistance</strong>. Over the centuries, it has survived colonization, stigmatization, and modernity.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, it continues to be a bridge between the past and the present, between nature and humans.</p>\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"descubre-el-per-u-aut-entico\"> Discover authentic Peru</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Exploring the culture of the coca leaf is entering the heart of deep Peru </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tradition, spirituality and ancestral knowledge await you.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> <strong>Travel with <a data-id=\"gtperutravel.com\" data-type=\"link\" href=\"http://gtperutravel.com\">GT Peru Travel</a> and live unique cultural experiences</strong><br/> Contacts: +51 920 185 267</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n",
